# Frontend bar (Nic) — win or nothing

14k teams. Cosmetics do not win.

## Every Nic frontend iteration MUST

1. Write in `docs/win-progress.md` **one game-breaking idea** for this loop (what a judge remembers in 10 seconds).
2. Ship **that idea only** end-to-end (code + copy + push if relevant).
3. Update progress honestly.

## Hard ban (do not spend a loop on these)

- Button / chip / accent color tweaks
- Spacing, radius, shadow, font polish alone
- Renaming labels without new capability
- “Make it prettier” / gradient / glass / glow for its own sake
- Tiny a11y or copy nits unless blocking a wow feature
- Refactors with no user-visible new power

## What counts as game-breaking (examples of bar)

- New way to **see motion** (compare, blink, trail, tour, measure)
- New **judge-ready** interaction (one-click story, shareable moment)
- New **discovery** affordance (spot the mover, predict vs observe)
- Wiring **new Tommy data** into a visible capability
- Shipping latest UI to **production/main** so judges see it

If the idea would not change a judge’s mind vs 14k other SPHEREx sites, **discard it** and pick a bigger one.
